# Corpus unit test-time-model-adaptation/C05 — gap (policy-mandatory variance CQ unmet; annotator optional)
#
# Source: test-time-model-adaptation C05 annotation (causal, component_ablation;
# corpus pin 62e9b54). Headline: activation-discrepancy fitness enables stable CMA-ES learning
# for online unsupervised TTA — on ImageNet-C severity 5 it lifts CMA prompt adaptation from
# 55.5% NoAdapt to 63.4% alone and 66.3% with activation shifting (best of all FOA variants),
# in contrast to the entropy-only failure (C04) (E05/E06, Table 5/Table 2).
#
# Lowering notes (conventions: corpus-units/LOWERING.md):
#   * component_ablation(C, S, Q, Exp), conclusion contributes(C, S, Q). The ablation ladder
#     (NoAdapt -> discrepancy-only -> + shifting) supports a positive contribution of the
#     discrepancy fitness.
#   * Policy-vs-annotation divergence (uniform-standard rule, as in adaptive-pruning/C03): the
#     mandatory variance_reported CQ maps onto the annotation's "is 'stable/consistent learning
#     signal' measured directly (variance, convergence traces, seeds)?", which the annotator rated
#     OPTIONAL and unmet-gap (metrics are endpoint accuracy and ECE only; no seeds or variance).
#     corpus-v1 makes variance mandatory family-wide (27 mandatory vs 16 optional annotations),
#     and the policy call wins: the incomplete argument is declared as a located hole with
#     `open variance_reported` (lowering re-done for issue #15 under `lara-core@0.3`), and
#     complete support stays empty. The claim's own "stable learning signal" wording is exactly
#     the unmeasured quantity, which sharpens the divergence.
#   * single_variable (mandatory) is annotated met (E05's 7-way ablation isolates the discrepancy
#     term); protocol_parity (mandatory) is supplied by the identical ImageNet-C severity-5,
#     15-corruption protocol across all variants and NoAdapt. Both leaves are supplied. The
#     optimizer-independence CQ (SGD) is optional-met, no effect.
#
# Expected verdict is at the bottom of this file (golden oracle).

artifact test-time-model-adaptation at sha256:59da7e38fd9f
policy corpus-v1
use backends [nd@1]

# --- The headline claim, stated but not assemblable at corpus-v1's evidential bar --------------

claim c05
  nl      = "On ImageNet-C severity 5 the activation-discrepancy fitness lifts CMA-ES prompt adaptation from 55.5 percent NoAdapt to 63.4 percent alone and 66.3 percent with activation shifting (best of all FOA variants), contrasting the entropy-only failure; stability is inferred from endpoint accuracy only, with no seeds or variance reported"
  formal  = contributes(activation_discrepancy_fitness, cma_es_prompt_tta, adaptation_accuracy)
  binding = { author = m0-annotator, audit-status = unreviewed }

# --- Evidence leaves are present ... ------------------------------------------------------------

# Principal premise: E05's ablation-ladder cells (55.5 -> 63.4 -> 66.3), per result cell.
leaf e1 : reports(e05, ablation_effect(activation_discrepancy_fitness, cma_es_prompt_tta, adaptation_accuracy, positive))
  kind       = observed
  provenance = ai-executed
  refs       = [logic/claims.md#C05, logic/experiments.md#E05, trace/exploration_tree.yaml#N08-N11, Table-5]

leaf e2 : isolated(activation_discrepancy_fitness, e05)
  kind       = attested
  provenance = ai-executed
  refs       = [logic/experiments.md#E05-Procedure-step-3, logic/experiments.md#E05-Procedure-step-5]

leaf e3 : matched_protocol(e05)
  kind       = attested
  provenance = ai-executed
  refs       = [logic/experiments.md#E05-Setup, logic/experiments.md#E06-baselines]

# --- ... and the incomplete argument is a located hole ------------------------------------------

# variance_reported(e05) has no honest leaf — endpoint accuracy/ECE only, no seeds or variance —
# so the policy-mandatory variance_reported stays open (the annotator rated it optional).
arg a1 : supports(c05) by component_ablation(activation_discrepancy_fitness, cma_es_prompt_tta, adaptation_accuracy, e05)
  discharge single_variable   with e2
  discharge protocol_parity   with e3
  open      variance_reported

status c05

# ==============================================================================================
